[Drop Decomposition]
  drop([C] SAE masked)     = -27.0
  drop([D] passthrough)    = -19.4  <- pure reconstruction noise
  masking_cost             = -7.6  <- extra cost from zeroing dead latents

  => Masking cost is NEGLIGIBLE. The dead latents genuinely carry no
     useful task information. SAE masking is principled -- the drop
     is driven by reconstruction noise, not incorrect feature removal.

  => Coord-basis masking is BETTER than even pure SAE passthrough.
     This means the reconstruction noise from the SAE is the primary
     bottleneck. The SAE approach needs better reconstruction fidelity
     before it can beat the simple coordinate-basis approach.

[Interpretation]
  XX Coord-basis masking is surprisingly better (26.3 pts).
  XX Possible causes: SAE reconstruction error corrupts Q-value decisions,
     or dormant neurons truly carry near-zero distributed activation mass.

  SAE stats: 946/1024 dead latents (92.4%) vs 144/256 dead neurons (56.2%)
